WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.137
Now the origin.

2
00:00:01.137 --> 00:00:04.175
Use Private Link where the
origin type supports it.

3
00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:09.696
Learn's page on Private Link in Front Door
Premium lists App Service, Blob Storage,

4
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:15.300
internal load balancers, API Management,
Application Gateway and Container Apps.

5
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.949
Approve the private endpoint
connection Front Door requests,

6
00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.388
and don't mix public and private
origins in one origin group.

7
00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.457
Where Private Link doesn't apply,

8
00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:29.516
Learn's page on securing traffic to Front
Door origins says to use the Front Door

9
00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:33.119
backend service tag and the X
Azure F D I D header together,

10
00:00:33.119 --> 00:00:37.412
because the tag's addresses are
shared by every Front Door customer.

11
00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:40.488
The header carries your own
profile's Front Door I D.

12
00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:44.449
For an App Service origin, one
access restriction does both,

13
00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:47.037
as Learn's multi-region tutorial shows.

14
00:00:47.037 --> 00:00:50.144
For an application
gateway behind Front Door,

15
00:00:50.144 --> 00:00:55.270
an N S G rule allows only the tag, and a
firewall custom rule checks the header.
